# Files a GENERATOR owns outright — never hand-edited, always rewritten whole.
#
# Bean `folio-assistant-1swy`. Measured 2026-09-24 over three days:
#
#   106 commits  cat-harness/docs/cat-harness/docs-auto/index/index.html
#    45 commits  cat-harness/docs/glossary/index.md            (1.5 MB)
#    18 commits  cat-harness/test/results/audit-coverage.qa-results.json
#
# Merging one branch cost THREE rounds on one of them in a single sitting. Every
# concurrent pull request pays a resolution round on a file that is regenerated
# from the whole corpus anyway, and every review carries a 1.5 MB diff nobody
# reads.
#
# ## Two attributes, both portable — no `git config` required
#
# `linguist-generated=true`  GitHub collapses it in review, so the diff stops
#                            burying the change somebody is actually reviewing.
# `-diff -merge`             git stops attempting a line-by-line merge on a file
#                            no human edits. The conflict is then ONE clean
#                            conflict to resolve by regenerating, rather than
#                            markers buried inside a megabyte.
#
# A merge driver that auto-resolved would need `git config merge.*.driver`, which
# is per-checkout: it would work here and nowhere else, including CI. Deliberately
# not that.
#
# ## Why this is safe, and it rests on a checked fact rather than on care
#
# All three are gated in CI — `check:glossary`, `docs:auto:check` and
# `audit:coverage:require-all`. A resolution that takes the wrong side therefore
# CANNOT SHIP: it reddens, and the repair is one regeneration command. Without
# those gates this entry would be a way to lose work quietly.
#
# ## What is deliberately NOT here, and it is the whole discipline
#
# **Not `cat-harness/test/results/**`**, though 840 generated files live there.
# `kg-audit` reads its own sidecars back — `readAttestations(sidecarPath(r))` —
# so a `kg-qa` sidecar carries adjudications that an earlier run or a person
# recorded. It is not purely generated, and `-merge` on one would discard an
# attestation with nothing said. `audit-coverage.qa-results.json` is named
# individually for exactly that reason: its producer reads the committed file
# only to compare for staleness, and writes a fresh document every time.
#
# So the test of whether a file belongs here is NOT "is it generated" but
# **"does its producer carry anything forward from the existing file"**. A glob
# over a generated directory is how the wrong answer gets in.
# `scripts/tests/gitattributes.test.ts` holds that line.

cat-harness/docs/glossary/index.md                      linguist-generated=true -diff -merge
cat-harness/docs/cat-harness/docs-auto/**               linguist-generated=true -diff -merge
cat-harness/test/results/audit-coverage.qa-results.json linguist-generated=true -diff -merge
